-- POWERS: PokeAPI reports no power for moves whose power is COMPUTED --
-- from weight, speed, HP, friendship, PP.  Gen 1 tracks none of that, so they
-- arrived at power 0 and dealt literally no damage (Beat Up was the reported
-- case).  Each gets a flat value near its practical average, or a Gen 1 effect
-- that captures the intent: Sheer Cold becomes a real OHKO, Final Gambit
-- becomes Explosion, Endeavor becomes Super Fang, Beat Up becomes a 2-5 hit.
--
-- EFFECTS: secondary effects mapped onto Gen 1's 82 effect constants.  Tiered
-- side effects pick the 10% or 30% variant from the real effect chance.
-- Multi-stat boosts keep their PRIMARY stat, because Gen 1 raises one stat per
-- move: Bulk Up raises Attack, Calm Mind raises Special, Dragon Dance raises
-- Attack.  Half a move beats no move and the flavour survives.
--
-- REMOVE: moves whose entire function is a mechanic Gen 1 does not have, with
-- no damage to fall back on -- abilities (Simple Beam, Entrainment, Worry
-- Seed, Skill Swap, Role Play, Gastro Acid), held items (Fling, Trick,
-- Switcheroo, Bestow, Recycle, Embargo, Natural Gift), weather (Rain Dance,
-- Sunny Day, Sandstorm, Hail), entry hazards (Spikes, Stealth Rock, Toxic
-- Spikes), turn order (Trick Room, Tailwind, After You, Quash), double-battle
-- moves (Helping Hand, Follow Me, Wide Guard), and protection (Protect,
-- Detect, Endure).  Keeping them as no-op buttons would be worse than not
-- shipping them: a move that visibly does nothing reads as a bug.
--
